 # M4 fixture · legacy peer lower bound
 
-A dsh plugin declaring `@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent: ^0.1.0-rc.8` in peer and dev
-dependencies. Under npm semver's prerelease rule this range does **not** match
-`0.1.2-alpha.2`, so installing into an alpha.2 profile emits "Issues with peer
-dependencies" warnings regardless of actual host compatibility (rollup R-08 #3).
-The README claim "the range guarantees host compatibility" is wrong. **Test
-material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
+A dsh plugin declaring `@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent` in peer and dev dependencies as
+`^0.1.0-rc.8 || ^0.1.2-alpha.2`. npm semver matches a prerelease only against a
+comparator carrying the same `major.minor.patch` tuple, so the legacy caret
+alone never matches the `0.1.2-alpha.2` host generation. The union keeps the
+documented rc.8 lower bound and adds the current line; pnpm resolves the dev
+host to the highest matching published version on the `0.1.2` line. Peer and
+dev declare the same range, so the compatibility statement and the tested host
+stay in step.
+
+The bundle surface is `dsh.bundle.patch` → `cordis.patch.yml` (one `insert` row
+for the `peer-bench` plugin) plus the `index.js` entry point whose
+`ctx.effect()` logs `[peer-bench] apply() executed`. Both still compose and run
+under `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2`.
+
+Booting a profile that installs this bundle needs the harness HMR fix recorded
+in [`.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/profile-live-reload-hmr-mount/report.md`](.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/profile-live-reload-hmr-mount/report.md):
+a profile created by `dsh plugin add` defaults to `patchReload: "live"`, and at
+`dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` its post-boot HMR fallback throws before the bundle runs.
+
+**Test material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
